/** @page openldapgettingstarted Getting Started

    @tableofcontents

    This page shows the fastest path to a working LDAP client with the Qore
    openldap module. See @ref openldapcookbook for full examples of every
    operation and @ref openldapsaslguide for SASL, GSSAPI, and hardened-bind
    configuration.

    @section openldapgettingstartedprereqs Prerequisites

    - <b>%Qore 2.0+</b> with @c %modern enabled
    - <b>OpenLDAP</b> client libraries installed (OpenLDAP 2.6+ is required
      for SASL channel binding — see @ref openldapsaslguide)
    - <b>Cyrus SASL</b> development headers — the module hard-depends on
      @c \<sasl/sasl.h\>
    - A reachable LDAP server and valid bind credentials
    - The @c openldap binary module loaded: @c %requires @c openldap

    @section openldapgettingstartedhello Minimal Example

    The example below connects to an LDAP server, performs a subtree search,
    and prints the results:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires openldap

LdapClient ldap("ldap://localhost", {
    "binddn": "cn=admin,dc=example,dc=com",
    "password": "admin",
    "timeout": 20s,
});

hash<auto> result = ldap.search({
    "base": "dc=example,dc=com",
    "filter": "(objectClass=person)",
    "scope": LDAP_SCOPE_SUBTREE,
    "attributes": ("uid", "cn", "mail"),
});

foreach string dn in (keys result) {
    printf("DN: %s\n", dn);
    printf("  cn: %s\n", result{dn}.cn);
}
    @endcode

    @note The @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient "LdapClient" class is thread-safe and
    wraps each request in a mutual-exclusion lock. For multi-threaded
    applications, the @ref openldaphelpermodules "LdapConnectionPool" helper
    module provides efficient per-thread connection reuse.

    @section openldapgettingstartednext Next Steps

    - @ref openldapcookbook — complete examples for every LDAP operation
    - @ref openldapsaslguide — SASL authentication and hardening
    - @ref openldaphelpermodules — connection pooling, async, LDIF, Active Directory
    - @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient "LdapClient class reference"
*/
